Task: Implement Retry.middleware (Green) — deviation documentation

Summary: Documents the real architectural deviation from the plan's literal wording:
Retry.middleware delegates its execution loop to http4s's own Retry client middleware
(which correctly handles Resource/Hotswap lifecycle for retrying a Client[F]), using
cats-retry's RetryPolicies purely for backoff computation under cats.Id. fullJitter
wasn't usable (needs effectful Random[F], incompatible with http4s's pure backoff
signature) — using limitRetries + exponentialBackoff instead. Logging goes through
purerest's own StructuredLogger[F] convention (via AttemptCountKey/onError), not
http4s's LoggerFactory-based internal logging (disabled via logRetries=false, with
NoOpFactory[F] to satisfy the required context bound).

